-- title:
--   Level automorphisms preserve supersingular maximal ideals of the j-chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be prime, $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of `levelH q M'`, the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K\subseteq L((\mathfrak q))$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`. Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly; let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of the $j$-series `jq`, and write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Assume, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, that each $\tau:K\simeq_L K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` maps $C$ into $C$; here that predicate says that for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ on the level group attached to $H_1$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero rational series, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the image of $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta=\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the $\iota$-image of the expansion of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k(\text{conjugate of }\gamma^{-1}\text{ by }\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q)$ equals that of $f\mid_k(\text{same conjugate})$. Fix such $\gamma$ and $\tau$, and a maximal ideal $y'\subset C$ containing $\varpi$ which is supersingular, in the sense that every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ into an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with kernel $y'$ sends $j$ into `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has trivial $q$-torsion. Then the preimage of $y'$ under the restriction of $\tau$ to $C$ is again maximal, contains $\varpi$, and is supersingular in the same sense.
--
--   This says that the level automorphisms of $K/L$ attached to elements of $\Gamma_0(M')$ permute the supersingular closed points of the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the finite $j$-chart of the integral model, the maximality and the supersingularity condition being transported along the pull-back. It is used in the later analysis of places of $K$ and of Igusa-type coordinates at such points, where a supersingular point must be moved by these automorphisms.
